# V's way-in, seat and R1 re-route (b8949c96, Nov 13 2026; ironspec 20:35 (2) (c), day-1 20:40)
# Frame: the module (loop) frame, as the (b+) file de143a70 and record7f13b. V's stop = 58f770cc's fold bfa0c8098 at loop = local + (0,-20,-1)
# (bed head (-3,-20,3), ENTRY (3,-18,-5), its torch (3,-18,-6) on glass (3,-19,-6): 58f770cc's cells, not listed here).
# Rule: today's way-in raised 4 above the drop (the queue (9,-14,-4) -> (9,-10,-4): the seat 17.154 from the head's centre, 9fc3155f's
# convention), the drop and the roll raised 7 (the roll at y -18 into ENTRY), R1's N group re-routed down to y -10 (day-1 20:40), the
# (C') hatch branch and the post dropped (day-1 20:40).
#
# REV 3 (Nov 14): + the leg's hold P1 (9,22,5); booster 1 (9,22,-4) and booster 2 (9,22,2), each always powered by a lit torch
# on a glass pane beside it; P1's exit detector (9,22,3) (day-1's token CLEAR); the resync detector (9,24,7) (its reader pending
# day-1: vestigial, it swaps back to the plain rail); the stop wall re-declared from real releases (pre-clip overlaps); the
# designed falls' exit speeds against the game's all-phase band; the column landing's first contact and rest; the arrival
# detector (9,-9,-5) as the front-clear evidence (ironspec 07:14 / 08:16a: the cover edge z -3.71, every ridden rest -3.8867).
# REV 2 (Nov 14 00:01): the designed falls say what stops each one horizontally, with the drop's footprint (ironspec 23:12, G1 23:06).
# REV 1 (Nov 13 23:05; rev 0 = a/1704449704371119, md5 0ba23333d45d, vcompose's part WAYIN): + glass (4,25,-2), the leg's
# sight guard (claimed 22:58, F3's withdrawn 23:02); - glass (4,-10,-6) and (5,-11,-6) (dropped 22:35); + the drop stop's two
# bounded contacts at their V cells (ironspec 21:57 (2): the same pair 4 higher); + the designed falls named (ironspec 22:33).
#
# The way-in's bounded contacts at V (the (b+) bounded copy's two lines moved up 4 with their cells; their figures are V's own
# ride rows on bplus3 + this delta laid over it, 1,640 rows, Nov 13 21:55: the same pair, the same depths and speeds):
# contacts: 9,-11,0=the way-in's drop stop at V: the launched cart meets the glass's north face off the rail end (9,-11,-2) and falls down the shaft (9,·,-1) on the next tick (one build position: a touching-contact bar, the set owed) | class=design | face=north | ticks<=1+eps=0 why=one tick a row (a second tick is the cart held at the glass) | events<=1+eps=0 why=one event a row | depth<=0.2057+eps=0.001 why=by the spread (0 over the reference's rows) | speed_in=0.4000+eps=0.001..0.4000+eps=0.001 why=the off-rail cap | speed_out>=0.1943+eps=0.001 why=by the spread | rate=1640/1640 rows | ref=b8949c96 V ride rows (bplus3 + this delta, 1da1826a0's reference command, 1,640 rows, Nov 13 21:55)
# contacts: 9,-12,-2=the rail end's support at V (glass): the launched cart, off the rail end the tick it meets the glass (9,-11,0) (the same move), rests its box flush on this block's top for that tick, its requested gravity step 0.0400 clipped to 0, then falls clear into the shaft (ironspec 15:52: REAL and DESIGNED; one build position: a touching-contact bar, the set owed) | class=design | face=up | ticks<=1+eps=0 why=one tick a row | events<=1+eps=0 why=one event a row | depth<=0.0400+eps=0.001 why=one gravity step, by the spread (0) | speed_in=0.4000+eps=0.001..0.4000+eps=0.001 why=the off-rail cap | speed_out>=0.1943+eps=0.001 why=by the spread | rate=1640/1640 rows | ref=b8949c96 V ride rows (bplus3 + this delta, 1da1826a0's reference command, 1,640 rows, Nov 13 21:55)
# (rev 3, ironspec 04:23 (2), G1 05:20 (3): the stop wall re-declared at the boosters' speeds, replacing the legacy line carried
# from the (b+) file's WAYLEG part. The figures are the contact rule's REQUESTED OVERLAP BEFORE THE CLIP (its `depth` key), from
# REAL RELEASES: the hold sweep's 148 ridden runs from every P1 rest with both boosters (exits 0.5995..0.7676; mctas R6 9f1877688,
# V rev 1 + the boosters, a/1528696769283358) and the leg train's unheld passes (0.9616 here; tick-exact's game reaches 1.0704),
# riders with AI. The game's POST-CLIP rest is FLUSH (tick-exact 04:56: least centre z -4.5100, the box face at the wall face
# z -5.000 at every speed to 1.07 b/t); a post-clip overlap is 0 by construction, so the pre-clip figure is the impact measure.
# The planter's W2 figures are dropped (its start state was no real release).)
# contacts: 9,22,-6=the way-in leg's stop wall: the cart off the line's end (9,22,-4) meets the glass's south face, is stopped horizontally (the game's post-clip rest flush at z -5.000) and falls the confined column at z -5 (one build position; every drop, held or unheld) | class=design | face=south | ticks<=1+eps=0 why=one tick a cart | events<=1+eps=0 why=one event a cart | depth<=0.2885+eps=0.001 why=the requested overlap before the clip, the largest over 148 ridden real releases (the unheld 0.96 pass 0.0162) | speed_in=0.4000+eps=0.001..0.4000+eps=0.001 why=the off-rail cap | speed_out>=0.0095+eps=0.001 why=the least over the releases | rate=148/148 carts | ref=b8949c96 hold sweep HC1 (R6 9f1877688, V rev 1 + both boosters), 148 ridden real releases, Nov 14 05:15
# contacts: 9,21,-6=the stop wall's lower glass: a cart that has begun to fall as it meets the wall touches this block's south face too (14 of 148 releases) | class=design | face=south | ticks<=1+eps=0 why=one tick a cart | events<=1+eps=0 why=one event a cart | depth<=0.1905+eps=0.001 why=the requested overlap before the clip, the largest over the 14 | speed_in=0.0000+eps=0.001..0.2000+eps=0.001 why=a falling cart's horizontal speed, halved on the ground | speed_out>=0.0095+eps=0.001 why=the least | rate=14/148 carts | ref=b8949c96 hold sweep HC1 (R6 9f1877688), Nov 14 05:15
# contacts: 9,21,-4=the line end's support (glass under booster 1): the cart's box flush on its top the tick it leaves the end (the same move), its gravity step clipped, then the fall | class=design | face=up | ticks<=1+eps=0 why=one tick a cart | events<=1+eps=0 why=one event a cart | depth<=0.0400+eps=0.001 why=one gravity step | speed_in=0.0000+eps=0.001..0.4000+eps=0.001 why=the off-rail cap | speed_out>=0.1115+eps=0.001 why=the least over the releases | rate=148/148 carts | ref=b8949c96 hold sweep HC1 (R6 9f1877688), Nov 14 05:15
#
# The designed falls (ironspec 17:02's form; tick-exact 22:29's pin: a cart landing in a rail cell never hurts its rider;
# ironspec 22:33: the arrival detector (9,-9,-5) is LOAD-BEARING (fragile), the cell above it (9,-8,-5) stays air; ironspec
# 23:12 / G1 23:06: each fall says what stops it horizontally):
#   the leg's column: the x-9 line's end at y 22 (9,22,-4) > (9,22,-5): the STOP WALL (9,22,-6) stops the cart's horizontal
#   motion (vz -> 0), so it falls the confined column at z -5: its FIRST CONTACT is the arrival detector (9,-9,-5) (31 blocks, a
#   rail landing; AL's case, tick-exact's game row: 20 / 20 seated), pressing it; it then rolls south down the detector's slope
#   onto the front's braked slope (9,-10,-4) and RESTS there at (9.500, -9.051, -3.887) (tick-exact's game row 03:33; the bench's
#   "waits in [9,-10,-4]"). The resting cart keeps the arrival detector PRESSED (its box reaches 0.177 into the detector's
#   search box, inset 0.2: powered 1,200 / 1,200 at rest, game-confirmed; the cover edge z -3.71 is the game's own; every ridden
#   rest over the 148 real releases at -3.8867, margin 0.1767; a perch rests deeper at -3.966..-3.980). The resting box reaches
#   0.377 into the column's cell, so P1 releases only when day-1's token is set AND the arrival detector reads UNPOWERED (the
#   front clear; ironspec 06:21 / 07:14): the token is set by the departure detector (9,-11,-3)'s press only after THIS napper's
#   own arrival press since the last release (ARRIVED, ironspec 07:38r), or by the recovery (ARRIVED and the arrival detector
#   unpowered for 30 gt, ironspec 08:41a); each release clears it. The departing box at the press (z -3.147..-2.167, rider
#   -2.957..-2.357) is 0.86 clear of the column footprint (z <= -4.01); the departure path is a point of no return (22 jam rows,
#   each met by the departing napper, 0 returns, 0 re-presses: R6 5a6b5fd7d, a/1680288200409008).
#   Its exit speed at the rail end (rev 3, ironspec 03:13 / 03:23 (6): every designed rail end judged against the game's
#   ALL-PHASE band, 0.27 empty / 0.25 ridden, tick-exact 03:09): with booster 1 alone the least RIDDEN exit is 0.4801 b/t (1.92x
#   ridden, 1.78x empty; tick-exact's y-22 row 03:33 to the 4th decimal); with both boosters 0.5995 (2.40x / 2.22x), every
#   landing still in the arrival cell (the stop wall confining the 0.7676 top speed); the least EMPTY exit with both 0.3878
#   (1.44x the empty 0.27); each measured at the first tick past the rail end (a conservative reading); the end geometry: the
#   last rail (the booster) on a full block over open air;
#   the drop: the rail end (9,-11,-2) > (9,-11,-1): every launch that clears meets the DROP STOP (9,-11,0) before it drops below
#   it (its horizontal motion stopped), so it falls the 1x1 shaft (9,-12..-16,-1) onto the landing booster (9,-17,-1) on
#   slime (9,-18,-1) (6 blocks, a rail landing over slime); its footprint one cell at every speed: R6's start-phase sweep
#   (687ade4a2), 0.001..0.450 x 10 phases: every speed from 0.2470 up clears, all 2,406 falls land in (9,-17,-1)'s rail cell,
#   the rider's least health 20.0 (a/1805815673978755); slower launches are held on the support and never fall; its exit
#   speed (rev 3, G1 03:34; ironspec 03:23 (6)): every normal launch leaves the rail end at 0.5789 b/t at the first tick past
#   it (the leg-train rows, R6 9f1877688; the rail-end cell's entry 0.4393 over the 1,640 ride rows), 2.32x the game's ridden
#   all-phase bound 0.25 and 2.14x the empty 0.27; a release whose launch is lost (the pile-up's perched napper, 0.1343)
#   strands on the support: a fault, in the guide's fault note;
#   the arrival slope's high side: (9,-9,-5) > (9,-8,-6) (air; clear of the pad): a fault path only (a cart going up the
#   arrival slope), not a normal-operation fall.
